From d2b77fa3df9c857618fe24d926fe997993d3e1a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 08:07:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-119: the IO lamp / panel button's own properties
 in the grid (0.119.0)

EastSun 20261001: "replicate the old version's functional architecture in the current one".
The old company components -- the IO lamps (TALed / TMyLed / TMyLedLane = span.aled) and the
panel buttons (TBtnPanel / TBtnPanelLane = div.btnpanel) -- showed only the ordinary
properties; their shape, lit / down and colours had to be changed in the HTML by hand.

Now they get a category of their own, "IO", with BCB6's names: a lamp LEDStyle (the six
shapes) / Value / Blink / TrueColor / FalseColor, a button Style (tsButtons / tsFlatButtons) /
Down / TrueColor / FalseColor / TrueFontColor / FalseFontColor. Each row is compared with the
.dfm (marked, reset from the marker, to the .dfm line / the HTML), the colours have the 16
colours, the eyedropper and a typed clRed. Shape / lit / down / flat are classes, written in
place (new htmledit.setClass -- setAttr would move the attribute to the tag's end); a colour
is its CSS variable (--led-on / --led-off / --bp-true / ...). The DFM difference list (reset
all to DFM) includes them too.

Tests: lib 165, smoke 193, panels all pass; the real VS Code layer could NOT run -- VS Code's
own update (CodeSetup, running since 05:41) holds its install mutex until VS Code is closed,
so no test instance can start. lib (dfmEditValues io, setClass in place, propRange), probe
(a lamp and a button: their values read, a shape = a class edit, a colour = --led-off, a
lamp's Down / a non-#rrggbb colour ignored), panels (both kinds' rows, Down differs from the
.dfm, Style / reset Down / clBlack sent, 6 shapes, none for an ordinary control), smoke (a
class edit written in place, taken out = the tag as it was).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
